---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  description="How create-stack handles analytics, consent, and privacy on the marketing site."
  title="Privacy · create-stack"
>
  <main class="privacy-page page-shell">
    <header class="privacy-intro">
      <p class="section-kicker">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Analytics with a clear boundary.</h1>
      <p>
        This page explains what the create-stack marketing site sends to PostHog and what it does
        not send.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: August 24, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Analytics is off by default</h2>
        <p>
          The site does not load PostHog until you choose "Accept analytics". You can refuse or
          change your choice at any time through the Privacy settings button.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we measure</h2>
        <p>After consent, the site sends a small set of events to the EU PostHog endpoint:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>page views and page leaves;</li>
          <li>copying the install command from the home page or stack builder;</li>
          <li>copying a stack share link from the stack builder.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The command text, project name, URL query string, form text, email addresses, and other
          user-entered values are not sent. Automatic click capture, dead clicks, session replay,
          surveys, and feature experiments are disabled.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Storage and withdrawal</h2>
        <p>
          The consent choice is stored locally. After you accept, PostHog may store an anonymous
          analytics identifier in your browser while analytics is enabled. If you withdraw
          consent, it stops sending events and removes the PostHog identifier stored by this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Provider and retention</h2>
        <p>
          PostHog processes the events for us through its EU endpoint. We aim to keep raw analytics
          events for no more than 12 months, with the project retention setting kept aligned with
          this policy. PostHog's own privacy and security information is available from
          {' '}
          <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>{' '}
          and{' '}
          <a href="https://trust.posthog.com/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">trust center</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For a privacy question or request, contact Alfred Mouelle at{' '}
          <a href="mailto:contact@alfredmouelle.com">contact@alfredmouelle.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
